# Spotter project rule

- Read `AGENTS.md` before changing code. Read the relevant document in `docs/` for cross-cutting work.
- Runtime code, Prisma schema/migrations, and tests are the technical source of truth. Report documentation conflicts; do not guess.
- Search for and extend existing implementations. Make the smallest compatible change and preserve unrelated working-tree changes.
- Preserve these invariants: Activity/check-in is not Workout; gym selection is optional; other gyms are viewable; chat is request → accept; privacy redaction remains strict; AI is available to all and makes no medical claims.
- Use `src/lib/apiClient.ts` for client API work and preserve server authorization/validation boundaries.
- Gym catalog edits must keep `src/data/gyms.json` and `api/prisma/data/gyms.json` identical; do not invent live counts.
- Update a `docs/` file only when changing a durable product rule, contract, architecture, operation, or UI convention. Add an ADR for significant decisions.
- Run relevant typecheck, lint, build, and tests; state clearly whether failures pre-existed.
- Never deploy, push, or change external state without explicit user authorization.
